---
import ProsePage from '../../templates/ProsePage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../config/site.ts';
import { routePath } from '../../i18n/routes.ts';
---

<ProsePage
  locale="en"
  routeKey="confirmed"
  noindex
  title="You are on the list"
  description="Your subscription is confirmed. Here is what you get and how often."
>
  <p><strong>That is it.</strong> Your address is on the list and there is nothing left to do.</p>

  <h2>What lands in your inbox</h2>

  <p>
    Three kinds of writing, and nothing else. All of it also lives on the site; the newsletter is
    the shortest way to it.
  </p>

  <p>
    A <strong>field report</strong> is an interview with someone building something here. We ask the questions
    and write it up. Often under the heading <em>People Who Build</em>, so the title tells you it is
    someone else speaking.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Release notes</strong> go out within ten working days of an evening: the slides, the photos,
    and what did and did not work. Including the second half. That is what turns an evening like twente.dev/001
    into an archive still worth something a year later.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Upstream</strong> collects what is happening in the region without us. Other groups, other
    evenings, other rooms. It claims nothing new and it invents no rhythm.
  </p>

  <p>
    You also hear when a talk slot is still open for the next evening, and when registration opens.
  </p>

  <h2>How often</h2>

  <p>
    There is no fixed cadence. A mail goes out when there is something worth saying. If a month
    stays quiet, nothing happened that month that you needed to know.
  </p>

  <p>
    Replies are welcome, there is a person on the other end. Every mail carries an unsubscribe link
    at the bottom, one click and no explanation needed.
  </p>

  <h2>In the meantime</h2>

  <p>
    <a href={routePath('blog', 'en')}>The archive</a> holds everything published so far. The
    <a href={routePath('events', 'en')}>calendar</a> is open to everyone and you can subscribe to it from
    your own calendar app. <a href={routePath('contribute', 'en')}>Contribute</a> lists what we could
    use help with right now: a story, a room, or an evening you know about that is missing here.
  </p>

  <p>
    Something wrong with your sign-up? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a
    >.
  </p>
</ProsePage>
